course: dictionary
lesson: 6835
title: Outdoor and indoor words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Outdoor is an adjective. It tells you that something happens, is used or is found outside, not inside a building. Outdoor games, outdoor shoes and outdoor clothes are all things you use outside. The related adverb is outdoors, as in "We played outdoors all afternoon."
explain: Look at the word parts: out and door. An outdoor game is one played out of the door, in the open air. Context helps too. In «outdoor shadows, such as on snow, often look blue or purple», the word outdoor tells you the shadows are in the open air, not in a room.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does "outdoor play" still make sense as "play outside"? Yes, so you have the right meaning. Inside a building is the opposite, so indoor is its opposite word.
fact: Outdoor means happening, used or found outside, not inside a building.
fact: Outdoors is the adverb. It tells you where something happens, as in "We played outdoors."
fact: «The great outdoors» means nature, the wild countryside away from towns.
fact: The redback spider hides in dry, sheltered places, which is why Australians check under «outdoor toilet seats» and «garden chairs».
fact: Outdoor safety comes first: wear sun cream and a hat in the sun, a coat in the cold, and always stay with your group.
exercise: «We have outdoor PE on Tuesdays, so bring your trainers.» What does outdoor mean here? | Very loud and noisy | Wet and muddy from the rain | *Outside, not inside a building | Inside the classroom
exercise: What is «the great outdoors»? | A large indoor swimming pool | A school hall | *Nature, the wild countryside outside towns | A shop that sells camping gear
exercise: «Take your shoes off, but keep your outdoor shoes by the door.» What are outdoor shoes? | The slippers you wear at home | The shoes you wear in bed | The shoes you wear to sleep in | *The shoes you wear outside, not indoors
test: What is the adverb form of outdoor? | Outdoorish | *Outdoors | Outdoorly | Outdooring
test: Which of these is an outdoor activity? | Watching TV on the sofa | *Climbing a hill with your group | Doing a jigsaw at the table | Reading a book in bed
exam: In cold weather, what is the best outdoor safety step? | Run off alone to explore | Take off your coat to feel cool | Go swimming in the cold lake | *Wear a warm coat and stay with your group
